  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppComm 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'After a new cancer treatment is approved, patients in your community
    share concerns about side effects they are experiencing at home. The side effects
    are minor, but they arose unexpectedly.


    <b>Community advocates can encourage
    patients and caregivers to report side effects so safety information continues
    to be collected after approval.</b>


    Is this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?'
  explanation: Community advocates help patients understand that safety monitoring
    continues even after a new treatment is approved. By encouraging patients to
    share their experiences, advocates help ensure side effects are reported and
    reviewed. This helps identify rare or long-term issues that may not have appeared
    in clinical trials and supports ongoing efforts to keep patients safe.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Approval
